  pxD_n: "For the finalists the presidential race multiplies their party's chamber vote (Lula 3.6×, Bolsonaro 2.2×). For Caiado it divides it (0.28×): 72% of the PSD electorate that voted for a PSD deputy abandoned Caiado presidentially; for Zema (NOVO) 89% did. That is lesser-evil voting measured on real ballots — the runoff's pressure acting already in round 1. Both map onto the 2022 center-right profiles whose transfer rows run 2:1 and 5:1 to Bolsonaro.",
